course: dictionary
lesson: 1258
title: Burning and safety
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Burning means being on fire, giving out flames and heat. «A smell of burning» is a warning, so tell a grown-up at once.
explain: Burning needs three things, the fire triangle: fuel, oxygen and heat. Take away any one of them and the fire goes out.
explain: The word also describes feelings and ideas. «A burning sensation» is a sore, hot feeling, and «a burning question» is a very important one. Look at the words around burning to find the meaning that fits.
fact: Burning means on fire, giving out flames and heat.
fact: Burning is an irreversible change: burnt wood cannot be turned back into wood.
fact: Burning fuel releases carbon dioxide.
fact: «Never throw water on a burning pan»: water sinks under the hot oil, turns to steam in a flash and throws burning oil everywhere.
fact: «Cool a burn under cold running water for 20 minutes.»
exercise: «A hot plug or socket, or a smell of burning, means an electrical fault.» What should you do first? | *Switch off at the wall if safe and tell a grown-up | Put water on the plug | Hide the plug somewhere safe | Keep smelling it to find out more
exercise: «Her eyes had a burning feeling after the smoke.» What does burning mean in this sentence? | Very old | Giving out light | Very cold | *Sore and hot
exercise: Can you get the wood back after it has been burning? | Yes, if you pour water on it | *No, burning is a change you cannot undo | Yes, if you wait a day | Only in summer
test: Which three things does a fire need? | Water, sand and ice | *Fuel, oxygen and heat | Light, sound and wind | Bread, milk and eggs
test: If your clothes catch fire, what should you do? | *Stop, drop and roll | Put on more clothes | Run as fast as you can | Wave your arms about
exam: A pan of hot oil catches fire in the kitchen. What is the safest thing to do? | *Never throw water on it, and tell a grown-up at once | Pour more oil on it to be safe | Carry it outside while it is burning | Throw a jug of water on it quickly
